    "body": "Thanks @dyfer \r\nCould reproduce it with remote server. All groups and synths created first are indeed needed, which is a quite complex node tree.\r\n\r\nThe crash is common to other situations calling abort or exiting program\r\n\r\naccording to\r\nhttps://github.com/supercollider/supercollider/blob/develop/server/supernova/dsp_thread_queue/dsp_thread_queue.hpp#L482\r\nthe specific issue is not the crash in this case but `poll_counts == watchdog_iterations` due to `fifo_empty` has happened too times.\r\n`fifo_empty` happens each time `runnable_items.pop(item)` returns false (which seems to happen on empty runnable_items)\r\n\r\nWhat does it really mean? I dont have the minimum idea!!\r\nIt seems that runnable_items would be empty if there are not running nodes for example (which is not the case as we dont get nova::dsp_queue_interpreter::run_item: possible lookup detected in dsp helper thread advise in this case)\r\nperhaps only @timblechmann understands this code.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
